{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|physics}} To emit [[electromagnetic radiation]], especially [[visible]] light, when [[absorb]]ing radiation of some other [[wavelength]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1974|author=John Boorman|authorlink=John Boorman|title=Zardoz|publisher=Pan Books|location=London|page=98|passage=The blinding light did not hurt, it filled him, he glowed, all his veins '''fluoresced''', each one alive with new growth.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} Of colours, to be very [[bright]]; to be so bright as to appear to radiate as a light source.

